{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22609 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "NRF2 activator Geopyxin F is implicated in the activation of the NRF2 transcription factor, which is known to regulate a wide range of stress-response genes. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which lead from Geopyxin F to SNU-387, a cell line that is subsequently targeted by various compounds, including 2-(hydroxymethyl)-3-[(E)-prop-1-enyl]phenol, sec-Butyl acetate, and (3S,7R,8Ar)-3-Benzyl-7-Hydroxyhexahydropyrrolo[1,2-A]Pyrazine-1,4-Dione. These compounds all ultimately target LS174T, suggesting a common downstream effect of NRF2 activation in this cell line. The evidence indicates that Geopyxin F may modulate NRF2 activity, leading to the activation of downstream targets that influence LS174T. The mechanisms are consistent with a direct interaction between Geopyxin F and the NRF2 pathway, as the observed targets are all known to be regulated by NRF2. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Geopyxin F and LS174T, highlighting the role of NRF2 in the regulation of cellular responses in this context.",
